<http://data.silknow.org/object/a93041cb-4bf7-3387-ba59-7dad5c8311b9>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric of brocaded silk, possibly made in England or the Netherlands, ca. 1734"@en , "Dress fabric of brocaded silk. With a design of islands with trees, flowers and houses. From the islands hang a large flower. With stags, birds and fruit. The green silk has a pattern weft bound on the surface in 1/3 twill as are all the other brocaded colours. The ground is a white tabby and is slightly ribbed. The selvedge contains stripes of brown (8 warp threads), white (10) and brown (10) edged by four cords of pink silk.\n\nThere is a comber repeat in the width of the material. Does not contain a full repeat in the height. The loom width between selvedges is 16.5 inches."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/a4c05237-c536-382f-aad3-e502cd8365eb> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of brocaded silk, possibly made in England or the Netherlands, ca. 1734"@en , "Dress fabric of brocaded silk. With a design of islands with trees, flowers and houses. From the islands hang a large flower. With stags, birds and fruit. The green silk has a pattern weft bound on the surface in 1/3 twill as are all the other brocaded colours. The ground is a white tabby and is slightly ribbed. The selvedge contains stripes of brown (8 warp threads), white (10) and brown (10) edged by four cords of pink silk.\n\nThere is a comber repeat in the width of the material. Does not contain a full repeat in the height. The loom width between selvedges is 16.5 inches."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/a93041cb-4bf7-3387-ba59-7dad5c8311b9/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/a93041cb-4bf7-3387-ba59-7dad5c8311b9/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.138-1969" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O261911> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/a93041cb-4bf7-3387-ba59-7dad5c8311b9/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress fabric of brocaded silk. With a design of islands with trees, flowers and houses. From the islands hang a large flower. With stags, birds and fruit. The green silk has a pattern weft bound on the surface in 1/3 twill as are all the other brocaded colours. The ground is a white tabby and is slightly ribbed. The selvedge contains stripes of brown (8 warp threads), white (10) and brown (10) edged by four cords of pink silk.\n\nThere is a comber repeat in the width of the material. Does not contain a full repeat in the height. The loom width between selvedges is 16.5 inches."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a93041cb-4bf7-3387-ba59-7dad5c8311b9> .

